"other", "confidence": "high", "qualifiers": [], "document_id": 
"20260729170222914331_c8c0a345", "claim": "When the Palace of Nestor burned c. 
1180 BCE, the clay tablets for their short-term administrative records were 
baked; preserving documents from the final year of occupation. During 
excavations under Carl W. Blegen between 1952-1964 CE, William A. McDonald 
discovered two rooms containing the largest collection of Linear B tablets 
found in one location, which was hence referred to as the 'Archive Complex.'", 
"text": "When the Palace of Nestor burned c. 1180 BCE, the clay tablets for 
their short-term administrative records were baked; preserving documents from 
the final year of occupation. During excavations under Carl W. Blegen between 
1952-1964 CE, William A. McDonald discovered two rooms containing the largest 
collection of Linear B tablets found in one location, which was hence referred 
to as the 'Archive Complex.'", "source_id": "20260729170222771555_7626eac3", 
"evidence_key": "evidence:c06822912598fe7930f8224b", "locator": "Pylos 
Archives", "status": "pending", "limitations": []}, {"id": 
"20260729170225296934_05d6921d", "type": "Evidence", "evidence_type": "other", 
"confidence": "medium", "qualifiers": ["The article states that the two new 
tholoi are not yet published."], "document_id": 
"20260729170222914331_c8c0a345", "claim": "The two new tholoi, although not yet
published, have yielded a gold pendant depicting the Egyptian goddess Hathor 
and a gold signet ring detailed with shoots of barley flanking two bovids. 
These two new artefacts signify a stronger connection with Egypt and the Near 
East than was previously understood.", "text": "The two new tholoi, although 
not yet published, have yielded a gold pendant depicting the Egyptian goddess 
Hathor and a gold signet ring detailed with shoots of barley flanking two 
bovids. These two new artefacts signify a stronger connection with Egypt and 
the Near East than was previously understood.", "source_id": 
"20260729170222771555_7626eac3", "evidence_key": 
"evidence:b6c55f0b390772269779902e", "locator": "Burials & Artefacts", 
"status": "pending", "limitations": ["The account is brief and does not provide
a separate provenance study for the ring."]}, {"id": 
"20260729170222914331_c8c0a345", "type": "Document", "text": "This article 
describes Pylos, a significant Mycenaean Bronze Age city in Messenia, Greece, 
and briefly mentions gold signet rings from the Griffin Warrior burial and 
nearby tholoi. It also summarizes the Palace of Nestor, its Linear B archives, 
burial landscape, and mythological associations with Neleus and Nestor.", 
"source_id": "20260729170222771555_7626eac3"}, {"id": 
"20260729170224871660_8459e4fe", "type": "Evidence", "evidence_type": "quote", 
"confidence": "high", "qualifiers": [], "document_id": 
"20260729170222894117_56afde57", "claim": "Hundreds of artifacts of gold, 
silver, bronze, ivory, and semiprecious stones were found with the body of a 
single male, 30-35 years old, dubbed the “Griffin Warrior.”", "text": "Hundreds
of artifacts of gold, silver, bronze, ivory, and semiprecious stones were found
with the body of a single male, 30-35 years old, dubbed the “Griffin 
Warrior.”", "source_id": "20260729170222742904_7a8d53d7", "evidence_key": 
"evidence:05bce3a22e967ee5cf083a9e", "locator": "Abstract", "status": 
"pending", "limitations": []}, {"id": "20260729170225642085_f4d4c52a", "type": 
"Evidence", "evidence_type": "quote", "confidence": "high", "claim": "In 2015 
there was an extraordinary discovery in Pylos (Messenia, Greece), of a rich 
unrobed grave called the grave of the Griffin Warrior... Among the many fine 
pieces of funerary equipment was a group of four gold signet rings and an 
intaglio gemstone made of agate, 3.6cm long, called the Pylos Combat Agate 
(referred to below as the PCA).", "qualifiers": [], "text": "In 2015 there was 
