"20260729170224320414_0d097437", "type": "Statement", "confidence": "high", 
"qualifiers": [], "text": "The article says the same combat scheme appears on 
several other seals, including the golden cushion seal from Shaft Grave III at 
Mycenae, the Battle in the Glen seal, a partially preserved seal of unknown 
origin, a seal from Tholos I at Gouvalari, a sealing from Ayia Triada, and 
another seal from Mycenae.", "source_id": "20260729170222830274_8de92d63", 
"document_id": "20260729170222961745_87c2902f", "statement_key": 
"statement:543efdcaa04bc2df308d8700", "limitations": []}, {"id": 
"20260729170223705632_b7f3800d", "type": "Statement", "confidence": "high", 
"qualifiers": [], "text": "The article says the Palace of Nestor was named 
after the Greek hero Nestor, that the earliest settlement at the site dates to 
c. 2000 BCE, that construction on the hill of Ano Englianos began c. 1600 BCE, 
that the structures burned c. 1400 BCE, and that the final palace stood until 
its destruction c. 1180 BCE.", "source_id": "20260729170222771555_7626eac3", 
"document_id": "20260729170222914331_c8c0a345", "statement_key": 
"statement:3390509f4ac299e20ccea7c4", "locator": "The Palace of Nestor", 
"limitations": []}, {"id": "20260729170222830274_8de92d63", "type": "Source", 
"source_type": "paper", "credibility_score": 0.5, "title": "COMBAT, MYTHS AND 
SEALS IN THE GRIFFIN ...", "url": 
"https://journals.akademicka.pl/saac/article/download/1109/949/1786"}, {"id": 
"20260729170223868525_8fadfba9", "type": "Statement", "confidence": "medium", 
"qualifiers": ["The article notes that these two new tholoi are not yet 
published."], "text": "The article says the two new tholoi next to Tholos IV, 
although not yet published, yielded a gold pendant depicting the Egyptian 
goddess Hathor and a gold signet ring detailed with shoots of barley flanking 
