"limitations": []}, {"id": "20260729170226544571_01740207", "type": "Conflict",
"conflict_type": "factual", "description": "The dating of CMS VIII no. 129 and 
CMS XII no. 292 is presented with two different chronologies: CMS assigns them 
to LB I-II, while Vonhoff dates them to LM IIIA/B and LH IIIA/B.", 
"resolution_status": "unresolved"}, {"id": "20260729170222937041_51b1f07e", 
"type": "Document", "text": "This article describes the Pylos Combat Agate 
(SN18-112), an engraved sealstone from the grave of the Griffin Warrior near 
the Palace of Nestor at Pylos, not a gold signet ring. The paper argues that 
the sealstone is likely a Cretan work of Late Minoan I and analyzes its 
discovery context, physical properties, combat iconography, and possible 
significance for the warrior's burial.", "source_id": 
"20260729170222801326_701795be"}, {"id": "20260729170223765678_fd9bb2d1", 
"type": "Statement", "confidence": "high", "qualifiers": [], "text": "The 
article says the Palace of Nestor burned c. 1180 BCE and that the fire baked 
the clay tablets, preserving administrative records from the final year of 
occupation; it also says excavations under Carl W. Blegen between 1952-1964 
uncovered the Archive Complex and the largest collection of Linear B tablets 
found in one location.", "source_id": "20260729170222771555_7626eac3", 
"document_id": "20260729170222914331_c8c0a345", "statement_key": 
"statement:0c2db3dd35fd68f2773a9e9d", "locator": "Pylos Archives", 
"limitations": []}, {"id": "20260729170224824969_e5dd2202", "type": "Evidence",
"evidence_type": "quote", "confidence": "high", "qualifiers": [], 
"document_id": "20260729170222894117_56afde57", "claim": "In May 2015, a 
University of Cincinnati team unexpectedly discovered a large stone-built tomb 
of Late Helladic IIA date near Tholos Tomb IV on the first day of renewed 
excavations at the Palace of Nestor, Pylos.", "text": "In May 2015, a 
University of Cincinnati team unexpectedly discovered a large stone-built tomb 
of Late Helladic IIA date near Tholos Tomb IV on the first day of renewed 
excavations at the Palace of Nestor, Pylos.", "source_id": 
"20260729170222742904_7a8d53d7", "evidence_key": 
"evidence:4b527e293718e1ddb3406cea", "locator": "Abstract", "status": 
"pending", "limitations": []}, {"id": "20260729170222961745_87c2902f", "type": 
"Document", "text": "This article discusses the Pylos Combat Agate and related 
gold signet rings from the Griffin Warrior tomb at Pylos (Messenia, Greece). It
argues that the repeated combat scenes on these seals may reflect a shared 
story or myth circulating in Late Bronze Age Greece, possibly with oral 
transmission and an ideological role among Mycenaean elites.", "source_id": 
"20260729170222830274_8de92d63"}, {"id": "20260729170224474988_4a9ac583", 
