"c:\\Users\\94498\\Desktop\\DeepResearch\\GraphResearcher\\outputs\\test_v5\\_r
uns\\82-Ring_of_Nestor\\.report_draft.md", "draft": "# Ring of Nestor\n\nThe 
Ring of Nestor is the name used in scholarship for a gold signet ring discussed
in connection with the 2015 Griffin Warrior burial at Pylos, Messenia, 
Greece.[1][2][3] The burial, found near the Palace of Nestor, contained a 
single male aged about 30-35 and hundreds of grave goods, including four gold 
signet rings decorated with Minoan ritual scenes.[2][3] The ring has attracted 
attention because its iconography has been analyzed in relation to Minoan and 
Mycenaean art and to debates about authenticity.[1][2]\n\n## Discovery and 
provenance\n\nIn May 2015, a University of Cincinnati team unexpectedly 
discovered a large stone-built tomb of Late Helladic IIA date near Tholos Tomb 
IV at the Palace of Nestor during renewed excavations at Pylos.[2][3] The tomb 
became known as the Griffin Warrior grave after the adult male buried there, 
who was accompanied by hundreds of artifacts made of gold, silver, bronze, 
ivory, and semiprecious stone.[2] Among the grave goods were four gold signet 
rings.[2][3] Pylos was one of the major Mycenaean centers in Messenia and the 
seat of the Palace of Nestor on the hill of Ano Englianos.[3]\n\n## 
Description, iconography, and interpretation\n\nA 2013 article by Theodore 
Eliopoulos, titled \"Some Observations on the Iconography of the Ring of 
Nestor,\" places the ring in the context of Aegean forgery and authenticity 
debates.[1] The broader Pylos find has been discussed alongside other Bronze 
Age glyptic objects, including the Pylos Combat Agate, which Stocker and Davis 
describe as a Cretan work of Late Minoan I found with other sealstones and four
gold rings near the warrior's right arm.[4] Their discussion and related 
scholarship compare the Pylos imagery with other Mycenaean and Minoan seals and
show that some related pieces have been dated differently in the 
literature.[4][5]\n\n## References\n\n[1] (PDF) SOME OBSERVATIONS ON THE 
ICONOGRAPHY OF THE ‘RING OF NESTOR’ 
https://www.academia.edu/83658257/SOME_OBSERVATIONS_ON_THE_ICONOGRAPHY_OF_THE_R
ING_OF_NESTOR_\n\n[2] (PDF) The Lord of the Gold Rings 
https://www.academia.edu/116392582/The_Lord_of_the_Gold_Rings\n\n[3] Pylos - 
World History Encyclopedia https://www.worldhistory.org/Pylos\n\n[4] The Combat
Agate from the Grave of the Griffin Warrior ... 
https://www.aegeussociety.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/Stocker-Davis-2017-Aga
te.pdf\n\n[5] COMBAT, MYTHS AND SEALS IN THE GRIFFIN ... 
https://journals.akademicka.pl/saac/article/download/1109/949/1786\n", 
